			"url": "https://ipn.arturia.com/products/hybrid-synths/keystep-37/overview"
		}
	],
	"abilities": [
		"Velocity-sensitive notes",
		"Channel aftertouch",
		"Arpeggiator",
		"Step sequencer",
		"Chord and scale modes",
		"Assignable MIDI CC banks"
	],
	"hardwareControls": [
		"37 slim keys",
		"Pitch and modulation strips",
		"Four assignable knobs",
		"Chord and MIDI CC buttons",
		"Display",
		"Clock-source DIP switches"
	],
	"notice": "This profile covers the original KeyStep 37, not KeyStep 37 mk2 or KeyStep Pro. Connect USB MIDI or DIN MIDI. Choose the clock source with the rear DIP switches and reboot after changing it. The four knobs have four configurable CC banks, so no fixed CC assignments are assumed. The virtual keyboard starts at note 48; match octave, scale and transpose using MIDI learn. USB port aliases have not been verified; select this profile manually. Diagrams are original schematics with illustrative positions, not scaled hardware drawings.",
